{"seq":2,"slug":"numbers","title":"拉姆齐数：算不出来的门槛","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/ramsey-theory/numbers","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"ramsey-numbers","title":"拉姆齐数 R(s,t)：算不出来的整数","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/ramsey-theory/numbers/ramsey-numbers","wordCount":1580,"readingTime":7},{"seq":2,"slug":"bounds-asymptotics","title":"上下界与渐近：夹缝里的 88 年","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/ramsey-theory/numbers/bounds-asymptotics","wordCount":1419,"readingTime":6},{"seq":3,"slug":"probabilistic-method","title":"概率方法：Erdős 的一页纸革命","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/ramsey-theory/numbers/probabilistic-method","wordCount":1587,"readingTime":7}],"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"拉姆齐数-算不出来的门槛\">拉姆齐数：算不出来的门槛</h1><p>基础一章证明了「足够大的结构必含秩序」，本章接手那个立刻冒出来的追问：足够大到底是多少？答案令人不安——存在性早已铁板钉钉，具体数值却几乎无从计算。本章就围绕这道鸿沟展开。</p>\n<p>第一篇给拉姆齐数 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R(s,t)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0077em;\">R</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">t</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span></span> 下严格定义，列出人类目前掌握的极少数确切值，并说明为什么 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R(5,5)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0077em;\">R</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">5</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">5</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span></span> 这样一个「五对五」的小问题至今只知落在 43 与 46 之间。第二篇转向界与渐近：Erdős–Szekeres 在 1935 年给出的上界统治了 88 年，直到 2023 年才被指数级击穿；我们会算清这些界的形状与常数。第三篇单独讲概率方法——Erdős 在 1947 年用「随机染色几乎必然无小团」这一招给出下界，开创了整个概率组合学，这一思想此后渗透进现代数学的每个角落。</p>\n<p>本章是全 hub 唯一系统处理「数值、界、渐近」的地方。基础一章不谈具体数字，推广一章把注意力移到别的染色对象，都会回指到这里。三篇内部也严格分工：确切值与定义归第一篇，上下界与渐近常数归第二篇，概率下界的方法论归第三篇，彼此只做一句话交叉引用而不重复展开。前置需要二项式系数、期望与基本不等式的操作能力。</p>\n"}